Hi all,

I am analysing a dataset from two camera-trap grids run in the same area. I ran Royle-Nichols occupancy models as well as single-season occupancy models, with co-varaites. For certain species, the R-N model offers significantly lower AIC values, which I have interpreted as meaning that differences in abundance between the two grids are affecting detection probabilities. However, I can't work out how to transform the R-N value (number of individuals per site) into an occupancy value. I also would like to test the goodness of fit of the R-N models, but can't find an equivalent of the mb.gof.test. Any help or guidance would be much appreciated.

An example of the output is included below. This is a model of distance to the boundary of the area as a whole and sub-sector of the area selected as the best model. The Distances have been back-transformed from their standardised values.

Kind regards,
Tom

